# ============================================================ 3. BRAND MASTER ASSETS

Create the canonical OX-DX master identity.

Required:

A. Primary logo

B. Symbol-only logo

C. OX-DX wordmark

D. Horizontal logo lockup

E. Vertical/stacked logo lockup

F. Monochrome black

G. Monochrome white

H. Dark-background version

I. Light-background version

J. Small-size icon

The core geometry must remain identical across variants.

Only color/background treatment may differ.

# ============================================================ 4. LOGO REQUIREMENTS

The main logo must work at:

16 × 16
24 × 24
32 × 32
48 × 48
64 × 64
128 × 128
256 × 256
512 × 512
1024 × 1024

It must remain recognizable at tiny sizes.

Do not create unnecessary micro-detail.

The symbol must communicate:

ontology
\+
relation
\+
resolution
\+
observation
\+
structure

without becoming a literal diagram.

The logo must work:

without the wordmark
with the wordmark
in monochrome
in a terminal
on GitHub
on a website
on documentation
on merchandise

# ============================================================ 5. SVG / VECTOR

SVG is the canonical source format.

Create clean, editable SVG files.

Required:

`ox-dx-logo-primary.svg`

`ox-dx-logo-monochrome.svg`

`ox-dx-logo-white.svg`

`ox-dx-logo-black.svg`

`ox-dx-icon.svg`

`ox-dx-wordmark.svg`

`ox-dx-lockup-horizontal.svg`

`ox-dx-lockup-stacked.svg`

`ox-dx-mark.svg`

Requirements:

- vector paths where appropriate
- no embedded raster image
- no unnecessary metadata
- no broken references
- no external font dependency
- no accidental clipping
- proper viewBox
- correct aspect ratio
- scalable to arbitrary size

The SVG files must render correctly independently.

# ============================================================ 6. VECTOR SYSTEM

Do not create only a logo.

Build a small supporting OX-DX vector language.

Create reusable vector primitives inspired by:

- nodes
- relations
- layers
- resolution
- grids
- observation
- signal
- transformation
- fragments
- geometric order
- nested structures

Create examples such as:

`resolution-grid.svg`

`relation-node.svg`

`layer-pattern.svg`

`observation-frame.svg`

`signal-fragment.svg`

`ontology-pattern.svg`

These are graphic primitives.

They must NOT be interpreted as new ontology semantics.

Do not invent additional ontology concepts.

