Create monochrome versions regardless of the accent palette.

The identity MUST work without color.

# ============================================================ 14. TYPOGRAPHY

Use the selected typography direction from the approved visual identity.

For vector assets:

avoid external font dependency.

For documentation of typography:

create a simple reference file:

`assets/documentation/technical/typography.md`

Document:

- primary display type
- secondary/body type
- monospace/technical type
- recommended hierarchy

Do not install proprietary fonts into the repository.

# ============================================================ 15. GRUNGE TREATMENT

Grunge is a surface layer.

It must NOT corrupt the core logo geometry.

Use grunge primarily for:

- hero
- banners
- backgrounds
- social preview
- section dividers

Possible treatments:

- subtle noise
- distressed texture
- photocopy texture
- scratches
- broken lines
- controlled distortion

Maintain high readability.

The logo itself should have a clean canonical version.

# ============================================================ 16. QURANIC VISUAL INFLUENCE

The visual influence should come through:

- mathematical symmetry
- geometric proportion
- repetition
- radial organization
- layered structures
- balance
- order emerging from complexity

Do NOT use:

- Quranic verses
- Arabic calligraphy
- invented Arabic text
- crescent symbols
- mosque illustrations
- religious iconography

The influence is philosophical and geometric.

