# ============================================================ 19. ASSET NAMING

Use deterministic lowercase filenames.

Format:

`ox-dx-{asset}-{variant}.{extension}`

Examples:

ox-dx-logo-primary.svg
ox-dx-logo-white.svg
ox-dx-icon.svg
ox-dx-hero-desktop.svg
ox-dx-hero-mobile.webp
ox-dx-footer-pattern.svg

No:

final-final.svg
logo-new2.svg
logo-last.svg
test123.svg

# ============================================================ 20. FILE FORMATS

Canonical:

SVG

Web optimization:

WEBP

General compatibility:

PNG

Do not generate JPEG unless genuinely necessary.

Preferred:

logos → SVG + PNG

icons → SVG + PNG

web graphics → SVG + WEBP

hero → SVG + WEBP + PNG

social → PNG + WEBP

# ============================================================ 21. QUALITY CHECK

After generating all assets:

Check every SVG.

Verify:

- valid XML
- valid viewBox
- no missing references
- no broken paths
- no embedded unwanted raster
- correct transparency
- correct aspect ratio

Check raster outputs.

Verify:

- correct dimensions
- correct transparency where needed
- no accidental crop
- no compression artifacts
- readable logo
- readable text

Check favicon.

Verify:

- recognizable at 16×16
- recognizable at 32×32

